      "notes": "MN 116:6.23 names Ānanda among the independent Buddhas. The verse counts twelve across three names. DPPN gives four named Ānanda with a commentarial citation. The verse does not identify the individual whose cremation Ānanda 06 describes. The citation for Ānanda 01 also lands on MN 116, but the attendant speaks in MN 115. DN 16 uses the name both for the attendant and for the shrine at Bhoganagara (ānande cetiye at 4.7.1 and 4.12.1). A single identification for DN 16 would mislabel some taps. AN 4.180:1.1 names the same shrine with the separately defined compound ānandacetiye. Its only standalone Ānando (10.2) is in the chapter summary and refers back to AN 4.174. Neither shrine passage names the yakkha himself. The identification in Ānanda 09 comes from the commentary. Its citation also lands on AN 4.178 and 4.179, neither of which names the shrine. The packet misses SN 45.19 and 45.20. In each, Bhadda addresses the elder as āvuso ānanda at 1.2, and the Pali repeats the address at 1.7. Sujato omits the name in both discourses. Untranslated chapter summaries also contain standalone forms outside the packet, for example AN 3.40:8.1 and SN 9.14:10.3."
